<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kanmon Straits</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Strait of Shimonoseki</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kanmon Straits are the narrow strait between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, linking the Inland Sea with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shimonoseki">Shimonoseki</a> on the north shore and Kitakyushu on the south. The naval Battle of Dan-no-ura in 1185 was fought there, and in 1863–1864 Western warships bombarded the Chōshū batteries that tried to close the strait. Today tunnels and a bridge cross it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kanmon-straits.jpg" alt="Kanmon Straits" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Image Science and Analysis Laboratory, NASA-Johnson Space Center · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kanmon_Straits_from_space_cropped_rotated_90_degrees_CCW.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
